    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to a student’s pace and understanding. They can explain concepts in various ways and offer practice problems tailored to individual needs. They can also act as virtual tutors, available anytime. This could reduce anxiety and make math feel less intimidating and more accessible to everyone."
